  "prefLabel": "Site 102.36 Presiding officer",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Site 102.36 “Presiding officer” means “presiding officer” as defined in RSA 541-A:1, XIV, namely, “that individual to whom the agency has delegated the authority to preside over a proceeding, if any; otherwise, it shall mean the head of the agency.”\n\nSource. #10993, eff 12-16-15 (from Site 102.15)",
